## nothing to say
(none)

## fast-forward suggestion
 - main is 3 commits behind origin/main; run wt --ff to fast-forward it.


## fast-forward suggestion, one commit
 - main is 1 commit behind origin/main; run wt --ff to fast-forward it.


## fallback notice
 - Git checked origin using `ls-remote`; this can take longer than the provider API.
 - Set GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN to let wt try the provider API, or use --ignore-api to use Git directly for this repository.


## suggestion before the notice
 - main is 3 commits behind origin/main; run wt --ff to fast-forward it.
 - Git checked origin using `ls-remote`; this can take longer than the provider API.
 - Set GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN to let wt try the provider API, or use --ignore-api to use Git directly for this repository.


## --ff refused: dirty checkout
 - main wasn't fast-forwarded: the checkout has uncommitted changes to files the update touches.


## --ff refused: diverged
 - main has diverged from origin/main, so it can't be fast-forwarded.


## --ff refused: missing local branch
 - main wasn't fast-forwarded: main doesn't exist.


## --ff refused: missing tracking ref
 - main wasn't fast-forwarded: origin/main doesn't exist.


## --ff refused: changed while waiting
 - main wasn't fast-forwarded: it changed while wt was updating it.


## --ff refused: git failed
 - main wasn't fast-forwarded: Git couldn't complete the update.
